{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/941971-2e-cofd-horror-and-supplemental-relevance","id":941971,"title":"2E/CofD Horror and Supplemental Relevance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-02T08:42:56-07:00","id":941971,"title":"2E/CofD Horror and Supplemental Relevance","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Couple questions for the community centered on how you guys are using the new editions so far (crossposted from the WhiteWolf reddit).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">First, as I was reading the books, I'm struck with just how buffed all the splats have gotten (werewolves are absolutely BRUTAL, and the changeling contracts are way beyond the sheer power levels they were at before compared to cost). When you're playing a mortal, that can definitely work in your favor, feeling helpless and vulnerable.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">When you're playing AS them though, how are you guys maintaining the sense of horror that should be part of this game? It can be hard to imagine being scared when you're an autohealing monstrosity that makes humanity literally mess itself, even when the enemies can do similar. I worry about the power creep a'la what I've heard out of the Supernatural crowd (the heroes are so powerful they can only be threatened by Satan's until-now unmentioned cousin Luciferisopheles who is more powerful than 10 satans!). I know making it personal can help, but how do you remove that veneer of &quot;we're badass enough to deal with this?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Secondly, obviously 1e had YEARS to build the material and give us NPCs and support and systems, etc. It feels a shame to leave all that in the dust if you're playing Chronicles. I adore some of the supplements like Autumn Nightmares and Pandora's Book. How are you guys utilizing the old support books? I'd love tips for translation or mechanical handwaving.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thanks in advance!</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2706-comicjunkie1","name":"comicjunkie1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:03:21-07:00","id":941989,"title":"","content":"The short answer: it doesn't matter how strong you are when the thing you're afraid of is yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:29:00-07:00","id":942009,"title":"","content":"I <i>have</i> been making plans to go into conversions for some of the Horrors found in the supplements. So far, I got a few of the primordial Horrors from Predators' third chapter, as well as most of the idigam in Night Horrors: Wolfsbane. As for the rest, I am sure some (especially the ones in Mage) are going to require a <i>lot</i> of reimagining to fit in with the 2E 'metaplot'.<br /> <br /> For instance, I'm still trying to figure out how to handle converting the Somnia Draconis from Night Horrors: The Unbidden. With Atlantis being thrown out the window (more or less), how do you imagine these golems being reskinned? Could they have their origins in the Hellenistic Era (just like the Diamond and the Seers)? Or do they perhaps originate from further down the past? Maybe even the time period of the Sundered World?<br /> <br /> Going back to topic, here's my answer for the <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;we're badass enough to deal with this&quot; </span></span></span>problem - Make the <i>bad guys</i> stronger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 08-02-2016, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:56:05-07:00","id":942026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/941971-2e-cofd-horror-and-supplemental-relevance?p=942009#post942009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, I'm still trying to figure out how to handle converting the Somnia Draconis from Night Horrors: The Unbidden. With Atlantis being thrown out the window (more or less), how do you imagine these golems being reskinned? Could they have their origins in the Hellenistic Era (just like the Diamond and the Seers)? Or do they perhaps originate from further down the past? Maybe even the time period of the Sundered World?</div> </div> </div> </div>But Atlantis <i>did</i> exist. Multiple of them. Thule, and Lemuria, etc. as well. And they didn't, too. I'd keep them as &quot;from Atlantis&quot;, except <i>which</i> Atlantis they are(n't) from keeps changing. Maybe even as you observe them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/941971-2e-cofd-horror-and-supplemental-relevance?p=942009#post942009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to topic, here's my answer for the <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;we're badass enough to deal with this&quot; </span></span></span>problem - Make the <i>bad guys</i> stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or drive home how the ability to punch through a truck, for instance, can't save your relationships. Or being able to rewire someone's mind does nothing positive for the question of &quot;am I a monster&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:38:01-07:00","id":942065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/941971-2e-cofd-horror-and-supplemental-relevance?p=942026#post942026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Atlantis <i>did</i> exist. Multiple of them. Thule, and Lemuria, etc. as well. And they didn't, too. I'd keep them as &quot;from Atlantis&quot;, except <i>which</i> Atlantis they are(n't) from keeps changing. Maybe even as you observe them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I guess that could work. Not to mention different Cabals will have different theories as to where the Somnia Draconis possibly hail from. Hmm. Maybe I should hold off on the fluff aspect of the conversion until Signs of Sorcery comes out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/941971-2e-cofd-horror-and-supplemental-relevance?p=942026#post942026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or drive home how the ability to punch through a truck, for instance, can't save your relationships. Or being able to rewire someone's mind does nothing positive for the question of &quot;am I a monster&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Chronicles of Darkness has no shortage of morally grey areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:42:39-07:00","id":942379,"title":"","content":"Well, I've always felt that the whole &quot;the x chronicle&quot; thing was partially to emphasize that there are Bigger Fish no matter how powerful you are. The Strix and Idigam are specifically designed to be formidable threats to Vampires and Werewolves, and are designed so that you can easily make your own to use as a BBEG or monster of the week. Mage kinda doesn't live up to this, but the less said about Awakening the better. <br /> <br /> Anyway, just keep the two principles that have been mentioned before in mind: Bigger Fish and Problems You Can't Solve By Killing Them. <br /> <br /> And about converting 1e stuff, it's not really that hard. The rules aren't that different. It's mostly a matter of streamlining and buffing. So, replace fiddly mechanics with Dread Powers or Numina when appropriate, and generally make things more powerful and dangerous. There have been some posts on the design philosophies of 2e that are helpful- like how Bloodlines in 2e are mostly leaving behind introducing new Disciplines, and instead go with an extra affinity discipline and a bloodline gift. So if you want to use a 1e bloodline, try making its Discipline (if it has one) into Devotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T22:10:07-07:00","id":942495,"title":"","content":"Power level has nothing to do with horror; it just changes the kind of horrors you can bring to bear. Weakness invites horror as an external force: look, everything out there is scary and terrible and it's coming for you. But strength invites a different horror, one where it's an internal struggle: look at what I can do, and look at the consequences of what I have done.<br /> <br /> Here's a thing I wrote up on rpgNet when people were asking &quot;what horror gameplay entails&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> For me? It's having enough carrots that your player is willing to do something terrible, and then having enough self-reflection that they can look back, from an OOC perspective, and find their character's actions repulsive. The subjective-stat mechanic is just a way, IMO, to <i>prompt</i> that self-reflection.<br /> <br /> Of course, the thing about horror is that it's supposed to leave you unsettled. That's part of the definition. So horror generally doesn't get placed at the end of things: it gets placed in the preparation and the lead-up, at most, and then the PCs go and clean everything up and make everything better and feel very good about themselves.<br /> <br /> But really where horror belongs, in an RPG? Is as a constant, inexorable temptation. You should constantly be finding reasons to do something terrible. It should be obvious, convenient, easy. You should be staring down the barrel of the gun, knowing all the time that it'd be simpler to just pull that trigger and kill that fucker. Let the Paradox go. Let Kuruth consume you. Let yourself Embrace him. Let yourself betray your motleymate. Choose to let go of humanity, just this once. It would solve the problem. It would solve it quickly, and efficiently, and damn the consequences. Move fast. Break things. That's what a PC does, right?<br /> <br /> That kind of horror can work at the session-level, I think, because all you have to do is find situations where there's a meaningful choice between something horrific but easy and something boring but difficult. And as a player, you get tired of doing the hard thing. Or you're bored of doing the right thing. So you take a dramatic failure. Or you choose to do the wrong thing. And you roll that subjective stat. You ask if it's worth it. Of course it is. You're bored; you're frustrated; you're willing to break a few eggs because this omelette needs to just be <i>done</i>.<br /> <br /> Suggestion: have your players write a diary entry about every roll they make against their subjective stat. Three or four sentences is enough; it's not supposed to be an essay. But have them really get inside their character's head, and figure out what that roll meant, internally, introspectively. Piece those entries together after the chronicle. Talk about them together. Talk about what your characters did, whether it was the right thing to do, if it was worth it.<br /> <br /> See if that helps you find the horror. Or, at least, see if it helps you find the self-justification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T15:20:41-07:00","id":943929,"title":"","content":"Depends on the gameline<br /> <br /> Werewolve, your afraid of your own rage and the posdiblity that you could kill someone you love when you lose control.<br /> <br /> Vampire: Your afraid of the emptiness within, so you hide in the echoes of your emotions and your plots.<br /> <br /> Mage: Smart Mages are afraid of the abyss, reapers, ect..., dumb ones are too stupid to be afraid.<br /> <br /> Promeathans are afraid of losing their shot at humanity and ending up eternally alone, till death.<br /> <br /> Hunter: Your basically mortal, sharing either fears.<br /> <br /> Changeling: Your terrified of going back, of the uber powerful True Fae and their minions, of see how much they've lost since being first taken to Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T18:53:51-07:00","id":944062,"title":"","content":"Mage: If you are new, you are afraid of Reapers, Banishers, the Abyss. If you are experienced, you are afraid of yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}